+++ b/src/lotus_v2/peer_codec_test/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,100 @@
+# Isolated V2 peer codec candidate
+
+This packet implements the reviewed proposal's byte codecs and compact-body
+reconstruction. It does not run a peer or change ABC's existing dispatcher.
+The caller supplies every network identity, magic, transaction profile, receive
+limit and local reconstruction quota. No development magic, ChainID, genesis,
+port, target, issuance or production profile is selected here. Test magic and
+identities are arbitrary test fixtures.
+
+Implemented:
+
+- Exact 24-byte TCP framing, inherited SHA256d checksum, printable command and
+  zero-padding checks, explicit payload/per-command caps, terminal framing errors
+  and fragmented-input decoding. `Feed` emits one message and reports input
+  consumption; callers must retain any remaining input. Length checks precede
+  payload allocation, and no allocation uses an unchecked announced length.
+- Exact 118-byte hello codecs, explicit identity/revision/required-feature
+  negotiation, min(local, remote) receive capacity, and the proposed canonical
+  BLAKE3 consensus-profile digest. Unknown supported features are ignored.
+- Native 134-byte V2 headers with one-byte zero sentinel (135-byte entries),
+  2000-header bound, 101-BlockID locators, 50000-entry inventory with full-TxHash
+  semantics for type 1, and sendcmpct framing. Unknown inventory types and compact
+  versions remain visible to the caller so it can ignore them explicitly.
+- Compact profile 2, shortest CompactSize framing, checked prefilled/request
+  deltas, prefilled coinbase at index zero, native complete transactions,
+  SHA256(Header || LE64(nonce)) keys and inherited SipHash-2-4 low-48-bit IDs.
+  No legacy CBlock or CTransaction conversion occurs.
+- One missing request per reconstruction; exact response ID/count/order and
+  complete-TxHash short-ID checks. A response for another BlockID cannot mutate
+  the current reconstruction. Same-ID malformed responses cancel their request.
+- Full-hash candidate deduplication, bounded collision buckets, ambiguity
+  requests, duplicate compact-short-ID fallback, and strict witness-variant
+  separation. Reconstruction verifies ordered transaction root, unique TxIDs,
+  first-and-only coinbase and exact complete block bytes. A root/size/core
+  mismatch requests a full block, never marks consensus invalid. Completion is
+  explicitly `CompleteUnvalidated` and must enter the common contextual block
+  validator.
+
+`NetworkProfile.max_reconstruction_transactions` bounds slot allocation, and
+`max_reconstruction_bytes` bounds the aggregate complete framed body before
+cached/response transactions are copied into slots. These are local quotas,
+not consensus limits. A byte/quota refusal from reconstruction means
+`NeedFullBlock`. A peer's claimed header size never authorizes allocating that
+size. Memory contains decoded transaction objects and temporary serialization,
+so this byte quota is not a claim of an equal resident-memory ceiling. Caller
+must also bound its existing cache, per-peer/global queues and retained codec
+objects. The decoder count checks use both available wire bytes and local caps;
+malformed requests cannot allocate a peer-declared count blindly.
+
+Functions returning bool leave their result unchanged on failure; error text
+classifies the failure for diagnostics. `EnvelopeDecoder` is stateful and
+terminal after a framing error. `CompactReconstruction` has explicit state
+transitions and `TakeComplete` consumes its result once. To replace an existing
+reconstruction, the caller starts a new one or calls `Cancel`; it owns request
+scheduling and timeout policy. Negotiation does not by itself activate relay.
+
+Not implemented in this packet (all remain transport/runtime integration work):
+
+- ABC version-70017 field codec, nonce self-connection checks, version/hello/verack
+  ordering, duplicate-handshake rejection, activation and 10-second timers;
+  parent integration must enforce these before dispatching application messages.
+- Sockets, connection lifecycle, datadir/network namespace isolation, disk magic,
+  address/addrv2 codecs/discovery, address databases, bans, peer selection,
+  ping/pong scheduling, quotas across peers, download queues and retries.
+- Headers-first synchronization, presynchronization, locators-to-chain lookup,
+  contextual target/PoW/parent eligibility, validated-chain service advertising,
+  persistent-state connection/reorg and atomic consensus validation.
+- Inventory batching, request tracking, full-TxHash tx-response verification,
+  notfound/capacity fallback scheduling, high-bandwidth compact announcement
+  permission, near-tip history/anti-amplification rules, and serving known-block
+  missing-index requests. Existing native transaction and block codecs supply
+  full-object framing; the dispatcher must enforce envelope capacity and request
+  identity before the common validator.
+- Optional unsupported-command/service disabling, fee policy, mempool/orphan and
+  witness-variant cache admission/replacement. Cached inputs supplied to `Start`
+  must already be complete and independently validated.
+- QUIC, TLS/ALPN, chunking or delivery of every economically valid P05 object.
+  Whole-object TCP capacity is deliberately finite. No public readiness claim.
+
+## Standalone verification
+
+```sh
+cmake -S src/lotus_v2/peer_codec_test -B /tmp/v2-peer-codec-build -GNinja \
+  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug \
+  -DLOTUS_SECP_LIBRARY=/absolute/path/to/libsecp256k1.a
+cmake --build /tmp/v2-peer-codec-build
+ctest --test-dir /tmp/v2-peer-codec-build --output-on-failure
+```
+
+Set `-DLOTUS_SANITIZE=ON` for AddressSanitizer/UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.
+The prebuilt archive is the existing ABC secp implementation; SHA256 and SipHash
+are compiled directly from the inherited ABC crypto sources. Chronik is absent.
+The standalone suite checks full/compact identical bytes and BlockIDs, exact
+identities, witness variants, deterministic ambiguity policy, duplicate short-ID
+fallback, incremental envelope splits, malformed lengths/counts/deltas/trailing
+bytes, wrong network/identity, absent witnesses, response association, exact
+root/size fallback and local capacity refusal. A 48-bit SipHash collision is not
+brute-forced: distinct candidate hashes exercise the actual uniqueness policy,
+and duplicated announced short IDs exercise reconstruction fallback. This is
+codec evidence, not live two-node or chain-validation evidence.
